<title>SPAIN: Spain budget allows &quot;more neutral&quot; money policy.</title>
<headline>Spain budget allows &quot;more neutral&quot; money policy.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato told Reuters Financial Television on Friday that the 1997 budget draft the cabinet just approved would allow for a more neutral monetary stance.</p>
<p>&quot;This budget allows for more neutral monetary policy,&quot; Rato told RFTV following a news conference on the 1997 accounts.</p>
<p>He also said he saw &quot;no danger of a rebound of inflation in 1997.&quot;</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
